# {{ .inputs.repo_name }}

{{ if .inputs.description }}{{ .inputs.description }}{{ else }}A hollis-labs class 2 Substrate service.{{ end }}

Class 2 tool (project/1 class model, RC1): `project.yaml` is the descriptor, `deploy.yaml` is read by `fleet-install`.

## Build

```sh
go mod tidy
go run github.com/hollis-labs/substrate/cmd/substrate pins sync --app .
go mod tidy
go build -o {{ .inputs.repo_name }} ./cmd/{{ .inputs.repo_name }}
./{{ .inputs.repo_name }} serve
```

## Deploy

`fleet-install deploy {{ .inputs.repo_name }} --commit <sha> --dry-run`, then without `--dry-run`. Set the host alias in `deploy.yaml` first.

## Run under Cerberus

Fleet-install places the binary; Cerberus only supervises it (`{{ .inputs.repo_name }}.cerberus.yaml`, no build, no artifact path):

```sh
cerberus validate {{ .inputs.repo_name }}.cerberus.yaml
cerberus register {{ .inputs.repo_name }}.cerberus.yaml
cerberus resource apply {{ .inputs.repo_name }} --ack
```

## Auth

Default `{{ .inputs.auth }}`. `enforce` needs a bearer token in `{{ upper (replace "-" "_" .inputs.repo_name) }}_TOKEN`. `{{ upper (replace "-" "_" .inputs.repo_name) }}_AUTH=loopback_open` is for development on a loopback bind only; the service refuses to start otherwise. `/healthz` names the active mode.
